gravity that differs from the traditional understanding in Einstein's General \
Relativity (GR). In GR, gravity is described as the curvature of spacetime, \
which is mathematically represented by the Riemann curvature tensor. \
Teleparallel gravity, on the other hand, conceptualizes gravity not as a \
result of spacetime curvature, but as a manifestation of **torsion** in \
spacetime.\\n\\n### Key Concepts of Teleparallel Gravity:\\n\\n1. **Torsion\"\
\>"], "Output",
